From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:46:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 75/78] texpacc: check that Exp(1) is exactly e on i386 and
 x86_64

Exp(1) must give 2.718281828459045 (bits $4005BF0A8B145769), the value
of the x87 Exp and of V8. On x86_64-win64 the SSE2 Exp gets it only
through its special case for 1.0 (fdlibm alone is 1 ulp above), so the
check fails without that and passes with it. Only i386 and x86_64 are
checked: other targets use the generic genmath.inc Exp, which has no
such special case. The argument is passed through BitsToDouble so that
the compiler cannot fold Exp(1.0) at compile time.
---
 tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp b/tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp
index 46c49477..b277b417 100644
--- a/tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp
+++ b/tests/test/units/system/texpacc.pp
@@ -84,6 +84,18 @@ begin
       lFailed:=true;
       end;
     end;
+{$if defined(cpui386) or defined(cpux86_64)}
+  { exp(1) must be e exactly (as V8 returns); the x87 Exp gives it, and the
+    SSE2 Exp of x86_64-win64 special-cases it (fdlibm alone is 1 ulp above,
+    so other targets using the generic genmath.inc Exp are not checked) }
+  lValue:=Exp(BitsToDouble(QWord($3FF0000000000000))); { not Exp(1.0): that is folded at compile time }
+  lGot:=DoubleToBits(lValue);
+  if lGot<>QWord($4005BF0A8B145769) then
+    begin
+    writeln('exp(1): got ',HexStr(lGot,16),', expected 4005BF0A8B145769 (e)');
+    lFailed:=true;
+    end;
+{$endif}
   if lFailed then
     halt(1);
   writeln('ok');
